---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { site, links } from '../site';
---
<Page title="About" description="Karl Sundström runs a one-person business in Stockholm building web scrapers, automations and verified datasets. What I do, how I work, and how to hire me.">
  <section class="intro">
    <h1>About</h1>
  </section>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I'm Karl Sundström. I run a one-person business (enskild firma) in
      Stockholm, Sweden. I build web scrapers, automations and datasets, and
      I write up how each one was made, including what broke.
    </p>

    <h2>What I can do for you</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Scrapers and data extraction.</strong> Before selling this I
        <a href="/blog/web-scraping-reality-check/">probed 150 sites</a> and
        published which ones can't be scraped reliably, so you'll get a straight answer up front.</li>
      <li><strong>Automations.</strong> Scripts and small agent pipelines that
        take a repetitive task off your plate.</li>
      <li><strong>Research datasets.</strong> Sourced, checked data where every
        row says how sure it is. See the <a href="/products/">products</a> for examples.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Some of my scrapers are also available ready-made on
      <a href="https://apify.com/vhsgreed">Apify</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>
      I work with AI agents, and I say so. I wrote down how and why in
      <a href="/blog/on-ai/">On AI</a>. Revenue comes only from what I sell:
      no investors, no ads.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Email is best: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      Tell me what you need and I'll tell you honestly whether I can do it.
    </p>
    <p>
      {links.map((l, i) => <>{i > 0 && ' · '}<a href={l.url}>{l.label}</a></>)}
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
